WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.730
In the question corner of Volume 105, the
author of One Piece dropped a bombshell about

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.830
Zoro’s lineage.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.800
We finally get confirmation that Zoro is in
fact related to the sword-god Ryuma that he

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.099
fought on Thriller Bark.

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:17.000
We also finally learn the identity of Zoro’s
long lost parents and even some shocking clues

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.660
that not just one, but TWO of the admirals
might be part of Zoro’s extended family.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.710
Starting with Zoro’s relation to Ryuma.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.170
Because when you look at the family tree,
you can see that Zoro got his name Roronoa

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.340
from his father.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.360
And it was actually his mother who is a direct
descendant of Ryuma and the Shimotsuki clan

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.360
of Wano.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.360
In case you didn’t know, we first learn
about Ryuma on the zombie island Thriller

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.360
Bark.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.930
During the final battles, Zoro duels and defeats
the animated corpse of the long dead samurai.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.500
Little did we know he was actually fighting
his ancient ancestor, which may explain why

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.239
Ryuma gave Zoro his famous sword Shusui after
being defeated.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:56.900
And while eventually Zoro returned this blade
during the Wano arc, now that we know Shusui

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.530
belonged to Zoro’s ancestor, we could see
him reclaim the famous blade before the end

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.530
of the story.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.350
But this is just the start of this ridiculous
family tree.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:13.120
We already knew that 55 years before the current
story a single ship escaped the samurai country

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.869
of Wano with 25 people on board.

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:22.710
Eventually this ship landed at a small village
in the East Blue, where the samurai of Wano

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.300
saved the village from bandits.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.100
This village later became Shimotsuki village,
the same place where Zoro learned how to fight

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.170
with the sword.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.460
And here is where the family tree branches
out.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.460
(here could either go with Kouzaburou first
or Zoro’s line first).

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.570
On this ship was Shimotsuki Kouzaburou, who
we first learned about from Kozuki Oden’s

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.049
father back in chapter 955 [show Tenguyama
or Sukiyaki].

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:46.490
He was a famous swordsmith who crafted two
of Zoro’s swords: the Wado Ichimonji and

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.490
Enma.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:51.200
We also recently learned that he was also
somewhat of a mentor to Zoro, as we see in

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:57.049
the flashback from chapter 1033, when he gives
Zoro two of his first actual swords that he

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:02.030
then used to challenge Kuina, Zoro’s first
rival and the person he made a promise with

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:06.100
to become the world’s greatest swordsmen.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.920
Kouzaburou married a girl from the village
and became the father of Koushirou, who was

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.400
the master of the dojo where Zoro trained.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.830
Koushirou later married and became the father
of Kunia,

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:21.780
But with the new information from the question
corner, as you can see here, we learn that

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.599
Zoro and Kuina were actually both a part of
the Shimotsuki family tree, though whether

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:31.700
they are direct cousins or more distantly
related is unknown.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.690
This takes us to Zoro’s direct lineage,
which is the most interesting part as it gives

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.920
us some incredibly juicy clues about Zoro’s
future.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.130
And you won’t believe what other powerhouses
in the one piece world might actually be a

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.360
part of Zoro’s family.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.769
But before we get into the juicy bits here,
I want to mention that while it is incredibly

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.900
exciting to learn more about Zoro’s past,
it is equally disappointing for me that we

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.970
are not learning about it in the main story.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:04.739
I mean, there were so many opportunities in
Wano to show this same information, but for

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:07.239
whatever reason Oda decided not to.

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:12.569
It is possible he thought it wasn’t important
enough, or maybe it was so important he wanted

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:18.910
to spend too much time on it, so it was eventually
cut in the prolonged chaos of Wano.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:24.900
Whatever the reason is, remember that Sanji
got TWO backstories, once during the Baratie

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:31.400
arc and once during Whole Cake Island, an
entire arc that was dedicated to his family.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:37.629
So I, for one, think that in the four years
we spent in Wano, we could have at least gotten

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:41.840
one chapter or so on Zoro’s past, even if
it’s just a side story.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:49.439
It would have made Zoro’s role in Wano even
more impactful, like the execution of his

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:51.860
relative Shimotsuki Yasuie.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.450
That being said though, let’s continue with
the family tree.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.469
Because there are some insane secrets we can
learn from Zoro’s family’s names.

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:02.010
Starting with Zoro’s grandmother, Shimotsuki
Furiko.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:07.180
Furiko was on the same ship that departed
Wano 55 years ago, and we are told in the

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.580
question corner that she is the older sister
of this guy [show Ushimaru], who we first

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.100
met in chapter 1024 during Yamato’s flashback.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:23.870
This guy is the former Daimyo of Ringo, Shimotsuki
Ushimaru, who for a while we thought was actually

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:24.930
Zoro’s father.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.630
It turns out he was just his great-uncle.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:32.620
And we’ve talked before on this channel
about Zoro’s future after they find the

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:37.690
One Piece, but since it is now confirmed that
Zoro was related to Ushimaru, do you think

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.720
that future Zoro could return to Wano to reclaim
his family’s former role as a daimyo?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.871
Let me know what you think in the comments
below.

00:04:43.871 --> 00:04:47.940
Continuing the family tree, Zoro’s Grandmother
Furiko married a swordsman from the Shimtosuki

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.820
village in the East Blue named Roronoa Pinzoro.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:56.280
Clearly Zoro was named after his father, so
we might as well call him Junior.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:01.889
And we can assume that Pinzoro and Furiko
are both dead, keep watching to find out what

00:05:01.889 --> 00:05:04.510
insane clues we learn from their names.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.080
Next we have Zoro’s father, Arashi.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.509
All we know about this man is that he has
spiky hair and that he died in a battle against

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:12.509
pirates.

00:05:12.509 --> 00:05:17.449
Which makes me wonder if he died protecting
the village or if he was a pirate himself.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:23.600
However, Zoro remembered enough about his
father to name an attack after him, Hana Arashi,

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.340
which we saw when he wielded Sogeking and
his sword together during the fight on Enies

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.340
Lobby.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.600
Arashi was married to Zoro’s mother Terra,
but similarly all we know is that she was

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.970
the daughter of thieving bandits and that
she died of some illness.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.699
Which seems to be a common fate for straw
hat character’s mothers since both Usopp

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:45.530
and Sanji’s mom’s also died of illness.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.740
Could Nami’s mom have suffered the same
fate?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:54.290
And with both of his parents dead, that leaves
our green-haired swordsman orphaned at the

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.310
Dojo in Shimotsuki village.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.900
And while that’s the end of the family tree
in the question corner, there is a lot more

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.100
that we can speculate based on the names of
Zoro’s direct family.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:11.330
Thanks to Sandman on twitter, it is clear
that Zoro’s family names are based off of

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.100
traditional Japanese dice gambling.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.349
Pinzoro, Zoro’s grandfather, means to get
double ones.

00:06:17.349 --> 00:06:21.050
Furiko, his grandmother, means a person who
rolls the dice.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:25.000
Arashi, Zoro’s father, means to get three
of the same number.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.250
And Terra is a possible connection to Tera-Zeni
or vigorish, which is a fee taken by gambling

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.250
companies.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:35.430
We even see that Zoro is fond of dice in Wano.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:41.319
In chapter 929, Yasu, who is actually Zoro’s
relative Shimotsuki Yasuie, claims that Zoro

00:06:41.319 --> 00:06:45.630
had just won a large sum from a dice gambling
house.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:51.900
Also, he often leaves things to chance, as
he did back in the sword shop in Logue Town

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:52.900
[ch 97].

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:58.120
But what is most interesting about this family
of dice gamblers is the other character who

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.620
might also share this connection with the
Shimotsuki family.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.229
Remember that back in Dressrosa, we are introduced
to this blind gambler, who turns out to be

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:08.270
the admiral Fujitora [ch 701].

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.729
And what is he gambling with…?

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:11.860
Dice.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.520
Seems like a pretty solid connections.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:19.319
Beyond this, Fujitora strongly resembles a
samurai and wields a traditional Japanese

00:07:19.319 --> 00:07:20.319
shikomizue.

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:24.740
We also know that Fujitora was born 54 years
ago, which was after the Shimotsuki ship left

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:31.180
Wano, so it makes sense that is out in the
world instead of still being stuck in Wano.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.599
We also know that he blinded himself at one
point because he had seen too many atrocities,

00:07:35.599 --> 00:07:40.849
so could it be that one day he returned to
Wano, saw the devastation left by Kaido, and

00:07:40.849 --> 00:07:43.710
then took the blade to his eyes.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:49.710
Another marine with ties to Wano, and possibly
the Shimotsuki, is Sentomaru, the bodyguard

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:50.819
of Dr. Vegapunk.

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:57.110
Sentomaru’s appearance is based on the japanese
folklore samurai Sakata no Kintoki and Sentomaru’s

00:07:57.110 --> 00:08:00.550
name is written in kanji, just like the people
of wano.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:04.990
So it’s possible he could be a descendant
of the Shimotsuki or another person who left

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.680
Wano 55 years ago.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:13.599
And if Sentomaru is from Wano, it is possible
another marine, this time the admiral Kizaru,

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:14.599
is as well.

00:08:14.599 --> 00:08:20.270
Kizaru speaks with a similar respectful, old
fashioned tone and Sentomaru even refers to

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:23.009
him with the honorific title Uncle.

00:08:23.009 --> 00:08:27.759
And the reveal of Zoro’s family tree of
course also added some fuel to the fire surrounding

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:28.849
the Marine Captain Tashigi.

00:08:28.849 --> 00:08:33.709
We’ve long known she looks strikingly similar
to Kuina [ch 100], and with all that we learned

00:08:33.709 --> 00:08:38.529
in this question corner, it is even more likely
that she is a Shimotsuki.

00:08:38.529 --> 00:08:43.420
She could have been another descendant of
Kouzaburou or another unnamed Shimotsuki from

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.420
that ship.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.060
And if this is the case, does Tashigi even
know that she is a descendant of the samurai

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.060
of Wano?

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:54.470
In fact, even Zoro and his childhood friend
Kuina are unaware of their famous ancestors.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:58.079
Which makes me wonder why no one ever told
them.

00:08:58.079 --> 00:09:02.350
Were their parents trying to protect them
from the marines or even keep Zoro and Kuina

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.769
from returning to Wano?

00:09:03.769 --> 00:09:07.680
While we don’t have those answers yet, if
you want to learn more about Zoro as a kid

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.769
and the true origin of his dream to be the
strongest swordsman in the world, you can

00:09:11.769 --> 00:09:15.649
watch this video about every backstory in
One Piece.

00:09:15.649 --> 00:09:17.319
Shanks for watching.

